{"title":"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67265ee7f4f72acdd2f3ee4e29c094832f573ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1, m_2, \\ldots, m_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"11\" /> be a collection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers, not necessarily distinct. For any sequence of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42a1cca8643e39135a3792d2d2b2ffe959af57df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (a_1, \\ldots, a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> and any permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/095a11d278599a8ef41ecaa13fd814d6ec4e26c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = w_1, \\ldots, w_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"11\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da2b6334b62a0a80483de87afa53f047ea8e391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1, \\ldots, m_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"11\" />, define an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />-inversion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> to be a pair of entries <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d85e21cfb9cabfbcb25a864136683112cd4282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_i, w_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/478f5d7d31a103e7a383486cdf317eb599ac9ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i &lt; j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> for which one of the following conditions holds:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e7a57a108c19f542380b6fa1beb50678c4c673.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i \\ge w_i &gt; w_j,\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f549c84bc48a26d35304ddc3d5ea8ff3bfdda743.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w_j &gt; a_i \\ge w_i,\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d846c7956ec8bfa8606414225de394a6712e90fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w_i &gt; w_j &gt; a_i.\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />\nShow that, for any two sequences of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42a1cca8643e39135a3792d2d2b2ffe959af57df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (a_1, \\ldots, a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfe719a9ba5369772ca2c411ea6826bb5101a514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (b_1, \\ldots, b_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />, and for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the number of permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da2b6334b62a0a80483de87afa53f047ea8e391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1, \\ldots, m_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"11\" /> having exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />-inversions is equal to the number of permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da2b6334b62a0a80483de87afa53f047ea8e391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1, \\ldots, m_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"11\" /> having exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />-inversions.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221111\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.007 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 65/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3761/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15565:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221111 and revision id 98888. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}